  "sourceSemantics": {
    "basic": [
      "getAmountsOut loops the exact route and can leave a hop amount zero when the derived address is not a recognized pool, so the workflow validates every hop and rejects partial/zero results.",
      "swapExactTokensForTokens enforces final output against amountOutMinimum, pulls from msg.sender directly into the first pool, and forwards intermediate output directly to the next pool.",
      "UNSAFE_swapExactTokensForTokens trusts caller-supplied amounts and is disabled."
    ],
    "concentratedLiquidity": [
      "exactInput paths encode token plus int24 tick spacing plus token; exact-output paths reverse the order and remain disabled.",
      "For exactInput multi-hop the first payer is msg.sender, intermediate output is held by the router, and later hops are paid by the router.",
      "The router has no standalone quote function; exact eth_call simulation is distinct from an estimate.",
      "Zero recipient means router custody and broad balance sweep/refund methods exist, so those entrypoints remain disabled absent separate composition review."
    ]
  }
